💭 A construction inside the right operand of 🤝/👐 must not corrupt the pending-registration tracking storage when
💭 the right operand is never evaluated because of short-circuiting. Before the fix, the tracking variable holding
💭 the pending receiver (or pending dynamic generic argument descriptions) was only initialized to null on the path
💭 that actually reaches the construction inside initObject(). Skipping the right operand left that variable holding
💭 an uninitialized value, which the checkpoint releaseTemporaryObjects() runs right after the 🤝/👐 merge could read
💭 and misinterpret as a live object to release.
